  "entry": "code/labbridge/app.py",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). A six-step Streamlit wizard that takes a messy plate-reader export, maps its columns to a standard schema with a person checking the choices, flags bad wells on a plate heatmap, runs scientific QC (standard curve, replicate CV, Levey-Jennings/Westgard control monitoring), gives a PASS/REVIEW/FAIL fitness verdict, and exports the cleaned dataset with a quality summary and transformation log. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
